# Data conversion between pebibyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between pebibyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1PiB to 1125.8999TB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PiB yields 1688.8498TB; backward, converting 1TB to 0.0008PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TB yields 0.0013PiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(PiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(PiB))

<<< stdout
1125.8999TB
1688.8498TB
0.0008PiB
0.0013PiB

<<< stderr
